  "summary": "5dive is a self-hosted multi-agent runtime where each agent is its own Linux user running an official coding CLI as a systemd service, coordinated through a single bash CLI over a shared SQLite task queue. Evidence covers the CLI surface, isolation tiers, delegated push, constitution loading, memory, UI, and a not-yet-shipped decentralized loop-install spec. Evidence coverage: 151 of 375 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
